remediation:
1. Configure Flask/Werkzeug to suppress version information in Server header by implementing a reverse proxy (nginx, Apache) that overrides the Server header with a generic value without version details.

2. Nginx configuration example:
   ```
   location / {
       proxy_pass http://backend;
       proxy_set_header Server "WebServer";
   }
   ```

3. Alternative: Use Flask extensions to override response headers and set a custom, version-agnostic Server header value.

4. Ensure production environment disables debug mode to prevent stack traces and other information disclosure vectors.

5. Consider implementing a Web Application Firewall (WAF) rule to sanitize outgoing Server headers.
